        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sa67",
          "text": "A brain injury can be mild, moderate, or severe. Mild brain injuries may result in little or no loss of consciousness. A severe brain injury may cause a long lapse in consciousness of a day or more. Brain injuries are not readily apparent; therefore, it is crucial to seek immediate medical attention after any head injury.",
          "marks": []
        }
